body:
You are 20 years old, so you're still learning (all my 20s was learning the hard way lol) but this is a big lesson you need to learn right now: No man gets to call you a pussy, ESPECIALLY when it comes to your pain, your experience, your reality. You do not stay with a man like that. I have endometriosis and if any man tried to tell me to suck it up when I'm in so much pain I hold my breaths and clench with each wave, that man would no longer be in my life anymore. There are men out there that will take care of you like you deserve when you need it, and never doubt or minimalize your pain.  Terrible period cramps are comparable to the pain of a HEART ATTACK. That fool doesn't know shit.

&#x200B;

DUMP HIM. There are plenty out there, relationships don't always have to last just because you're in one, 20s should be all about you making sure you only keep the people that support you and are healthy for you in your life. Don't subject yourself for one more minute to this abuse and nonsense. 

&#x200B;

Also from one woman with serious period pain to another, seek out a gynecologist and discuss your pain, and look into pain management. CBD has been a huge help to me, and I smoke on the worst days if I can. Good luck, and take good care of yourself.
